        example: "def compute_mvp_weights(sd1, sd2, rho):\n    cov12 = rho * sd1 * sd2\n    var1 = sd1 ** 2\n    var2 = sd2 ** 2\n    \n    # Analytical derivation: d(var_p)/dw1 = 0\n    # w1* = (var2 - cov12) / (var1 + var2 - 2*cov12)\n    numerator = var2 - cov12\n    denominator = var1 + var2 - 2 * cov12\n    w1_star = numerator / denominator\n    w2_star = 1.0 - w1_star\n    \n    # Portfolio variance and std dev at MVP\n    var_mvp = (w1_star**2)*var1 + (w2_star**2)*var2 + 2*w1_star*w2_star*cov12\n    sd_mvp = var_mvp ** 0.5\n    return w1_star, w2_star, sd_mvp\n\nsd_A = 0.137083\nsd_B = 0.015811\nrho_AB = -0.738549\n\nw_A_mvp, w_B_mvp, sd_mvp = compute_mvp_weights(sd_A, sd_B, rho_AB)\nmean_A = 0.14\nmean_B = 0.07\ner_mvp = w_A_mvp * mean_A + w_B_mvp * mean_B\n\nprint(f\"Minimum Variance Portfolio (MVP) Optimal Weights:\")\nprint(f\"  Weight in Asset A (Equities): {w_A_mvp*100:.2f}%\")\nprint(f\"  Weight in Asset B (Bonds):    {w_B_mvp*100:.2f}%\")\nprint(f\"Portfolio Expected Return:      {er_mvp*100:.2f}%\")\nprint(f\"Portfolio Volatility (Std Dev): {sd_mvp*100:.2f}%\")\nprint(f\"Comparison: Bond Alone Volatility was {sd_B*100:.2f}%\")\n",
