        output: "Anti-Takeover Mechanism                | Strategic Governance Mechanism\n===================================================================================================================\nPoison Pill (Shareholder Rights Plan)  | Flips-in discounted shares to existing holders upon hostile stake breach (e.g., 15%), inflicting massive economic dilution on the raider.\nStaggered (Classified) Board           | Only 1/3 of directors stand for election annually, delaying raider board takeover by at least 2 proxy voting cycles.\nCrown Jewel Defense                    | Firm sells or spins off its most profitable core operating subsidiary to destroy the strategic acquisition rationale for the hostile bidder.\nWhite Knight Defense                   | Target invites a friendly strategic corporate partner to outbid the hostile raider, preserving incumbent executive management.\nGolden Parachutes                      | Massive multi-million-dollar severance guarantees triggered upon change of control, inflating acquisition overhead for the hostile acquirer.\nPac-Man Defense                        | The target company turns around and launches a hostile tender offer to acquire the hostile bidder's own common shares.",
